# Copy this file to .env.linkedin-mcp (gitignored) and fill in your value.
#
# ⚠️  SECURITY — READ FIRST
#   - The li_at cookie is a FULL LinkedIn login credential. Anyone who has it
#     is logged in as you (no password or 2FA prompt).
#   - Keep the real file private:  chmod 600 .env.linkedin-mcp
#   - Never paste it into chats, issues, screenshots, or AI tools.
#   - If it is ever exposed, rotate it: log out of LinkedIn (Settings → Sign out
#     of all sessions), which invalidates the cookie, then log in again.
#
# ⚠️  NOT PART OF THE EXTENSION
#   This file is only for the separate, optional LinkedIn MCP server. That
#   server can send messages and connection requests automatically. That is NOT
#   part of this extension (which never posts or sends anything) and automated
#   messaging/connecting is against LinkedIn's User Agreement.
#
# Get LINKEDIN_COOKIE from your browser:
#   1. Log into linkedin.com in Chrome
#   2. Open DevTools -> Application -> Cookies -> https://www.linkedin.com
#   3. Copy the value of the "li_at" cookie
LINKEDIN_COOKIE=
